## 2. DEFINITIONS

**"You"** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License. If You act for an entity, You must be authorized to accept these terms on its behalf. Its employees, contractors, and automated agents may exercise the licensed rights on its behalf and under its responsibility; no separate seat fee applies.

**"Product"** means a game, application, tool, or service that You make available to others, or develop for that purpose, and that incorporates, loads, links to, or otherwise executes any part of the Software's code to provide its functionality. This includes execution on a server serving the Product, whether or not the Software is delivered to end users. A modification of the Software remains Software for this definition.

**"Distribute"** means to provide copies to another person or entity or make a Product's functionality available to them over a network. Internal use by people acting on Your behalf under this License does not, by itself, create an externally distributed Product.

**"Asset Outputs"** means models, meshes, images, textures, audio, animations, other creative resources, and generated files that do not incorporate covered Software code or require that code at runtime. Their creation, conversion, compilation, or export using the Software does not, by itself, make them Products. A work using only these outputs is likewise not a Product under this License, regardless of the number, proportion, or importance of those outputs. Separate rights in included Example Content or third-party material still apply.

**"Example Content"** means Etcito-provided example objects, sounds, other creative assets, game templates, and the original example gameplay code supplied with those templates, identified as examples in the repository, its notices, or file headers. It excludes the Etcito libraries and runtime components that those examples import, link to, bundle, or execute.

**"Gross Revenue"** means worldwide revenue directly attributable to a covered Product, calculated under Section 5 before deduction of platform commissions, publisher shares, payment-processing charges, development costs, or other business expenses.

**"AI Spend"** means the amounts You, or anyone acting on Your behalf, pay or incur for artificial-intelligence services and compute used to design, develop, produce, test, operate, or provide a covered Product, calculated under Section 5.8.

